+---
+id: task-003-return-single-use-coupon-on-cancel-confirm-free-shipping-at-50.00
+type: task
+title: "Return single-use coupon on cancel; confirm free shipping at 50.00"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Request
+
+1. A customer's single-use welcome code was refused as already used after cancelling the order that used it.
+2. A customer paid €4.90 shipping on goods of exactly €50.00.
+
+## Done
+
+1. Cause: `OrderService.cancel` gave the coupon back with the customer name instead of the order id, so
+   the coupon was never released. Fixed in `src/orders.ts`; test added.
+2. Not reproducible: the `>=` threshold was already fixed in task-001. Added a regression test for goods of
+   exactly €50.00 through order placement. If it recurs, the goods were probably below €50.00 after discounts.
